'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 12''' was the twelfth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on October 28, 2026 at the Kurosaki Prefectural Arena in [[Kurosaki]] — the first repeat market in the series' history, returning to the Episode 2 city four months later. The show opened the road to [[Power Struggle 2026|Power Struggle]] and was headlined by IGO Heavyweight Champion [[Leoni Masua]] ending [[The Marauder]]'s undefeated Wednesday night streak in a non-title main event, closing with a wordless message from G1 winner [[Marcus Vance]].

== Background ==

One week after the mutiny at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 11|Episode 11]] — the Usos out, the [[Cannon Club]] dead, Kengo alone — the Wednesday product entered its second season: the Power Struggle build. The storylines entering Episode 12:

* '''The gold under the dead banner.''' [[Kai Nakamura|Kai "The Flash" Nakamura]] and [[Danny Viggo|El Phantasma]] still held the [[IGO Junior Tag Team Championship]] — the last Cannon Club asset — with the faction that gave it to them no longer existing.
* '''Kengo's descent.''' Abandoned by everyone and beaten by Tama Uso, the founder of the Cannon Club had one claim left: the property.
* '''Jusuf's demand.''' The [[IGO Intercontinental Championship|Intercontinental Champion]] wanted a "real" challenger for Power Struggle, "or I stop showing up."
* '''The tag division.''' [[Kuroshio (stable)|Kuroshio]] — KAZUKI and Daigo Kuroki, whole again — were the presumptive challengers to [[Diego Reyes]] and [[Haruto Kimura]], and the champions knew it.
* '''The champion works.''' Leoni Masua's first match since the G1 — against the Marauder, 3-0 in singles on Wednesday nights and never beaten on the product.

