== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' The opener — the young ace against the wall. Diallo's power controlled the early minutes; Ono's speed and belief took the rest. The Ono Driver at 10:36. '''Crowd:''' '''ONO''' chants. HEAT for Diallo's shortcuts.
* '''Match 2:''' Malo's singles run rolled through the fallen Tanaka — the former television champion's brawling had its moments, but the pop-up Samoan drop at 11:44 was the family exclamation. '''Crowd:''' '''MALO''' chants. HEAT for Tanaka. The Kurosaki crowd — the series' first repeat market — loud all night.
* '''Match 3:''' The junior tag titles — the young lions' shot, one week after the non-title upset at Episode 11. Iwata and Yamamoto had the champions beaten twice; both times the Phantasma found the ropes or the tights. The Flash Flood never came — instead Viggo flash-pinned Yamamoto with a fistful of tights and both feet on the middle rope, unseen, at 14:12. The champions retain, dirty. '''Crowd:''' dueling chants, then NUCLEAR HEAT for the pin. '''BULLSHIT''' chants — the first of the series' second season.
* '''Match 4:''' The television title. Sato, CHAOS's second-generation technician, answered the open challenge and took Ishida to his craft — and to the Ishida Lock, center ring, at 12:08. The '''eighth''' submission of the reign. Handshake after — the champion honors the challengers he breaks. '''Crowd:''' '''ISHIDA''' chants. Respect applause for Sato.
* '''Match 5:''' The family's belt against the man who betrayed the family. Kengo's shortcuts and the referee's warnings kept it alive; the Samoan driver at 15:27 ended it clean. And then the descent went from sad to dangerous: Kengo took the chair from ringside and laid Taumafa out — two shots across the back, one across the head, the Strong Openweight Champion left in the wreckage. Officials pulled Kengo away; he did not resist. He smiled. '''Crowd:''' '''TAUMAFA''' chants through the match. SILENCE at the chair shots — then the loudest HEAT of the night. '''KENGO''' is now a curse word in three prefectures.
* '''Match 6:''' The main event — the champion's first match since the G1, against the undefeated Wednesday night mystery. The Marauder's power was real: the big boot staggered Leoni for the first time all season, and the guardrail throw drew gasps. But the Spear of Fangatapu — out of nowhere, mid-charge, at 13:19 — ended the streak. The Marauder's first Wednesday night loss. '''Crowd:''' '''WHO ARE YOU?''' chants early, '''LEONI''' chants late. MEGA POP for the Spear. The mask stood up before the ten — and walked out without an answer, again.

== Segments ==

* '''The dead banner (after Match 3):''' Kengo walked to the ring — alone — and made his claim over the junior tag gold: ''"That gold is Cannon Club property. And I am the Cannon Club."'' Kai Nakamura took the mic: ''"The club died at the Dome. The gold is ours."'' Viggo raised his belt without a word. The champions renounce the dead banner and keep the belts — free agents now. Kengo left without an answer, and without an army. '''Crowd:''' POP for Nakamura's line. A '''NA NA NA GOODBYE''' serenade as Kengo retreated.
* '''The Power Struggle announcement (mid-show):''' In-ring podium, the November card begins. NOPW announced the Intercontinental Championship match: [[Jusuf Muntasir]] (c) against '''[[Nakamura Shinsuke]]'''. Jusuf appeared on the stage, belt on his shoulder, and gave the artist his welcome: ''"An artist. Art is a lie with good lighting. In November, I turn off the lights."'' '''Crowd:''' HEAT — and the uncomfortable quiet underneath it.
* '''The tag war turns violent (before the main event):''' During a backstage interview, Diego Reyes and Haruto Kimura jumped KAZUKI and Daigo Kuroki — the champions' frustration going physical. The brawl was pulled apart, and the match was made official on the spot: '''Kuroshio versus the tag champions, for the IGO Tag Team Championship, at Power Struggle.''' '''Crowd:''' HEAT for the ambush. '''KUROSHIO''' chants from the building as the teams were separated.

== Main event close: One more man ==

After the Spear, as Leoni stood over the Marauder with the championship raised, [[Marcus Vance]] walked out — no music, no microphone. He stood at the top of the ramp. He looked at the champion. And slowly, deliberately, he raised one finger.

One more man.

He turned and left. Leoni watched him go and said nothing. Ten Wednesdays to Toyozawa.

'''Crowd:''' ERUPTION. '''VANCE''' and '''LEONI''' chants overlapping. The building on its feet.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Power Struggle card takes shape:''' Jusuf (c) vs. Nakamura Shinsuke for the Intercontinental Championship; Kuroshio vs. Reyes & Kimura (c) for the tag titles; Taumafa (c) vs. Kengo, the rematch nobody wants sanctioned, now written in chair marks; and the junior tag champions owing Iwata & Yamamoto a clean shot.
* '''The dead banner renounced.''' The junior tag gold stays with Nakamura and Viggo — as free agents. The last Cannon Club asset is no longer Cannon Club property.
* '''Kengo's descent.''' From abandoned to dangerous in one chair. The family war has a third act.
* '''The champion works.''' Leoni's first match since the G1, over the product's undefeated mystery. The table holds.
* '''The Marauder, answered.''' Beaten for the first time on Wednesday nights — and still nobody knows who he is.

